`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Budget limits are spend caps an org admin configures. They come from three places, and OpenRouter checks them in this order on every paid request, so the first one that is spent is the one that blocks:`}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Guardrail budgets`}),`: a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_usd`}),` with a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`reset_interval`}),` on the workspace default guardrail (checked against the member’s combined spend, then against the key’s own spend), on the guardrail assigned to the member, and on the guardrail assigned to the API key. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/features/guardrails`,children:`Guardrails`}),`.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Workspace budgets`}),`: caps on the whole workspace’s spend per interval. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/features/workspaces/workspace-budgets`,children:`Workspace budgets`}),`.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`The key’s own limit`}),`: the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit`}),` field above, once its window is spent.`]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Spend windows are UTC: a daily budget resets at 00:00 UTC, a weekly one on Monday 00:00 UTC, a monthly one on the first of the month 00:00 UTC. A lifetime workspace budget never resets.`}),`
