`]})})}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The budget applies to prepaid accounts spending their own credits, and only to a subset of them: accounts whose balance is below a threshold, and, while the mechanism is being rolled out, newer accounts without an established spending history. A larger balance raises the budget up to the ceiling, and a balance at or above the threshold is not subject to it at all. It does not apply to requests to free models, to requests served entirely with your own provider keys (see `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/overview/auth/byok`,children:`BYOK`}),`) that use no paid plugins, or to enterprise, paid-subscription, or invoice-billed accounts.`]}),`
`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`handling-402-errors`,children:`Handling 402 errors`}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To resolve `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{code:HTTPStatus.S402_Payment_Required})}),` errors:`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsxs(_components.strong,{children:[`Check `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`error.metadata.limit_source`})]}),` in the response body. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openrouter_in_flight_budget`}),` means your running and recently completed requests filled your `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`#in-flight-spending-budget`,children:`in-flight spending budget`}),`, not your balance: wait for the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Retry-After`}),` header and retry. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openrouter_key_limit`}),` means the API key’s credit limit is exhausted. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openrouter_credits`}),` means your balance cannot cover the request, or the single request is too expensive for your in-flight budget.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Add credits`}),` to bring your account balance above zero, or to raise your in-flight spending budget.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Check per-key limits.`}),` If `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_remaining`}),` on the key is exhausted, raise the key’s credit limit or wait for it to reset (see `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_reset`}),`).`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Reduce the request size`}),` (fewer input tokens or a lower `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`max_tokens`}),`) so its estimated cost fits your balance and in-flight budget.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Monitor proactively.`}),` Call `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` as shown above to track `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_remaining`}),` and usage before requests start failing.`]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`2`,id:`budget-limits`,children:`Budget limits`}),`
`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Budget limits are spend caps an org admin configures. They come from three places, and OpenRouter checks them in this order on every paid request, so the first one that is spent is the one that blocks:`}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Guardrail budgets`}),`: a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_usd`}),` with a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`reset_interval`}),` on the workspace default guardrail (checked against the member’s combined spend, then against the key’s own spend), on the guardrail assigned to the member, and on the guardrail assigned to the API key. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/features/guardrails`,children:`Guardrails`}),`.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Workspace budgets`}),`: caps on the whole workspace’s spend per interval. See `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/features/workspaces/workspace-budgets`,children:`Workspace budgets`}),`.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`The key’s own limit`}),`: the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit`}),` field above, once its window is spent.`]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsx(_components.p,{children:`Spend windows are UTC: a daily budget resets at 00:00 UTC, a weekly one on Monday 00:00 UTC, a monthly one on the first of the month 00:00 UTC. A lifetime workspace budget never resets.`}),`
`,_jsx(Heading,{level:`3`,id:`checking-your-budgets`,children:`Checking your budgets`}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` lists every budget that applies to the key in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`budgets`}),`, with the spend enforcement counts against it, how much is left, and when the window rolls over. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`effective_budget`}),` is the budget that blocks requests first: when one is already spent it is the entry enforcement rejects on (the first in the order above, or the broadest spent workspace budget), otherwise it is the entry with the least `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remaining_usd`}),`. `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_remaining`}),` keep describing only the key’s own limit.`]}),`
