`,_jsxs(Table,{children:[_jsx(_components.thead,{children:_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Credits purchased (all time)`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Requests per minute`}),_jsx(_components.th,{children:`Requests per day`})]})}),_jsxs(_components.tbody,{children:[_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`Less than `,FREE_MODEL_CREDITS_THRESHOLD]}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:FREE_MODEL_RATE_LIMIT_RPM}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:FREE_MODEL_NO_CREDITS_RPD})]}),_jsxs(_components.tr,{children:[_jsxs(_components.td,{children:[`At least `,FREE_MODEL_CREDITS_THRESHOLD]}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:FREE_MODEL_RATE_LIMIT_RPM}),_jsx(_components.td,{children:FREE_MODEL_HAS_CREDITS_RPD})]})]})]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`free_model_daily_requests`}),` field in the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` response above reports the daily counter and ceiling that gate your free-model requests when these limits apply to your account. Accounts and endpoints exempt from free-model limits, and BYOK requests, are not gated by it, so `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`remaining`}),` reflects the tier policy rather than an enforced ceiling for them. The per-minute limit is not reported there. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit`}),` tier is selected by all-time credits purchased, independently of `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`is_free_tier`}),`. To absorb rounding and top-up fees, the higher daily ceiling is granted starting one credit below the table’s threshold (currently `,FREE_MODEL_CREDITS_THRESHOLD-1,` credits); an account that has purchased fewer credits than that reports `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`is_free_tier: false`}),` together with the lower daily ceiling.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{start:`2`,children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Key-management limits`}),`: Creating, updating, and deleting API keys with a `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/overview/auth/management-api-keys`,children:`management key`}),` count toward a daily limit for your account or organization. The limit is 10,000 requests per day by default, and it resets at 00:00 UTC.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`POST /api/v1/keys`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PATCH /api/v1/keys/{hash}`}),` (including disabling a key), and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`DELETE /api/v1/keys/{hash}`}),` all count toward the same limit. A request counts even if it then fails, for example with a 404 for an unknown key.`]}),`
`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`Reading keys, usage, or credits doesn’t count toward it.`}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`When you reach the limit, requests fail with `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{code:HTTPStatus.S429_Too_Many_Requests})}),` until the reset. The `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`X-RateLimit-Reset`}),` header gives the reset time in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`If you create a short-lived key for each job, set `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`expires_at`}),` when you create it instead of deleting it afterward. This halves the requests that count toward the limit.`]}),`
`,_jsx(_components.li,{children:`If your workload needs a higher limit, contact support.`}),`
`]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Per-IP burst limits`}),`: These endpoints also limit how many requests each client IP address can make per minute:`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Key writes: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`POST /api/v1/keys`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PATCH /api/v1/keys/{hash}`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`DELETE /api/v1/keys/{hash}`})]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Key reads: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/keys`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/keys/{hash}`})]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Current key and credits: `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/credits`})]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Each endpoint counts separately, except that `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`PATCH`}),` and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`DELETE`}),` on `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`/api/v1/keys/{hash}`}),` share a count. The limits for key writes are lower than the limits for the other endpoints. These responses don’t include `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`X-RateLimit-*`}),` headers, so wait a few seconds and retry with exponential backoff.`]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`DDoS protection`}),`: Cloudflare’s DDoS protection will block requests that dramatically exceed reasonable usage.`]}),`
