`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`A `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{code:HTTPStatus.S429_Too_Many_Requests})}),` error can come from two places:`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ol,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`OpenRouter`}),`, when you hit one of the platform limits above (free-model requests per minute or per day, key-management requests per day, per-IP burst limits, or DDoS protection).`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`The upstream provider`}),`, when the provider serving your request is rate limiting or at capacity. In this case `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`error.metadata.provider_code`}),` carries the provider’s original error code when available, and `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/routing/provider-selection`,children:`fallback routing`}),` retries other providers for the same model automatically before the error reaches you. You can also specify `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/routing/model-fallbacks`,children:`fallback models`}),` to try a different model when all providers for the first are exhausted.`]}),`
`]}),`
`,_jsx(Note,{children:_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`Successful inference responses do not include `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`X-RateLimit-*`}),` headers. When OpenRouter itself returns a `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{code:HTTPStatus.S429_Too_Many_Requests})}),` error for a free-model or key-management limit, the error response carries `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`X-RateLimit-Limit`}),`, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`X-RateLimit-Remaining`}),`, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`X-RateLimit-Reset`}),` headers describing the limit that was hit. When every attempted provider returned a retry hint, the error response also carries a `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Retry-After`}),` header. To monitor your remaining free-model daily quota before hitting a limit, call `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` as shown above. It doesn’t report the key-management limit.`]})}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.p,{children:[`To resolve `,_jsx(_MdxComponentBoundary,{name:`StatusCode`,children:_jsx(StatusCode,{code:HTTPStatus.S429_Too_Many_Requests})}),` errors:`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`Retry with exponential backoff.`}),` Rate limits are transient; wait and retry rather than immediately re-sending. Honor the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Retry-After`}),` header when present.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`On free variants`}),`, purchase at least `,FREE_MODEL_CREDITS_THRESHOLD,` credits to raise your daily limit, or switch to the paid variant of the model, which has no platform-level request cap.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.strong,{children:`For provider-side limits`}),`, add `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/routing/model-fallbacks`,children:`fallback models`}),` or relax `,_jsx(_components.a,{href:`/guides/routing/provider-selection`,children:`provider routing preferences`}),` so more providers are eligible to serve the request.`]}),`
