`,_jsxs(_components.ul,{children:[`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`limit_source`}),` is `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openrouter_guardrail_budget`}),` for a guardrail budget, `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openrouter_workspace_budget`}),` for a workspace budget, and `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`openrouter_key_limit`}),` for the key’s own limit.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`scope`}),` matches the `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`scope`}),` values in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),`, so you can find the same entry in `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`budgets`}),`.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[_jsx(_components.code,{children:`resets_at`}),` is the ISO 8601 UTC instant the window rolls over, or `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`null`}),` for a lifetime workspace budget. Retrying before it will fail the same way; there is no `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`Retry-After`}),` header because the wait is usually hours or days.`]}),`
`,_jsxs(_components.li,{children:[`Call `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`GET /api/v1/key`}),` before a long task and watch `,_jsx(_components.code,{children:`effective_budget.remaining_usd`}),` to avoid hitting the cap partway through.`]}),`
